WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.869
Speaker 1: So we haven't talked about&nbsp;
vaccination for a while, and you know, generally&nbsp;

00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:08.880
Speaker 2: speaking, I've been aware
Speaker 1: that the U.S. has vaccinated about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:15.440
60 percent overall. And I intuitively assumed that&nbsp;
there was some kind of Partizan split because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.960
some of the numbers we've been looking at, but I
Speaker 2: did not realize&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.040
Speaker 1: how
Speaker 2: disturbingly horrible&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.200
Speaker 1: the Partizan gap is. So let's&nbsp;
go through what we've known for a while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.440
We've known for a while that there was&nbsp;
probably some Partizan split on vaccination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:38.400
We've seen that for the greater part of 2021.&nbsp;
COVID cases, hospitalizations and deaths have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.600
been disproportionately happening in the
Speaker 2: reddest red Trump&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:49.360
Speaker 1: counties compared to the bluest blue&nbsp;
Biden counties. We've seen how the COVID death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.520
rate since vaccines have been widely available is
Speaker 2: about three&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.480
Speaker 1: times higher in&nbsp;
the reddest Trump counties&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.720
Speaker 2: compared to the bluest Biden counties.
Speaker 1: And again, this came with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:07.120
intuition that part of the explanation must be&nbsp;
vaccination rates. Now, I also have said even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:13.029
in blue counties, it's likely that the deaths&nbsp;
are still skewing towards Republicans relative&nbsp;

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:15.600
Speaker 2: to that county's
Speaker 1: population. We now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.920
have data on vaccination, and it is even&nbsp;
worse than I imagine at this point in time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:30.400
96 percent of Democrats say they've already been&nbsp;
vaccinated, while only 54 percent of Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:38.080
have been vaccinated. There is no. There is&nbsp;
no lesser vaccinated group than Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:44.320
at this point in time in the United States.&nbsp;
Democrats are getting vaccinated at nearly twice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:50.880
the rate of Republicans. This is no small detail.&nbsp;
This is from polling done by Monmouth University.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.440
Let's take a look at the numbers in more&nbsp;
detail. So you see the clear Partizan divide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.560
96 percent of Democrats have been vaccinated,&nbsp;
79 percent of independents have been vaccinated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.400
and a pathetic 54
Speaker 2: percent of Republicans&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.920
Speaker 1: have been vaccinated. Now, just as&nbsp;
interestingly, 30 percent of Republicans say they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:19.760
will never get the vaccine. Another interesting&nbsp;
thing those who are not registered to vote.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.840
Actually got vaccinated at a slightly higher rate
Speaker 2: than those who are&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.600
Speaker 1: registered
Speaker 2: to vote. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:34.880
interesting. Also along educational&nbsp;
lines, there is a gap. 87 percent of those&nbsp;

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.560
Speaker 1: with a four year&nbsp;
degree have been vaccinated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:46.880
Only 73 percent of those without a four year&nbsp;
degree have been vaccinated, so not a big shock.&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.560
Speaker 2: Education leads to vaccination,
Speaker 1: just like education tends to lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.040
to people being more liberal, voting more&nbsp;
for Democrats than from Republicans. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.720
interestingly, there is almost no income gap&nbsp;
whatsoever. You might speculate you might not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.720
I don't know, but you might speculate that among&nbsp;
different income groups, you would see vaccination&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.440
Speaker 2: at different
Speaker 1: levels. The vaccine is&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.680
Speaker 2: free at the
Speaker 1: end user point, but maybe there would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:19.120
be some reason why you'd see different levels of&nbsp;
vaccine uptake based on income. We don't see that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.560
you make under 50k a year, 78 percent have been&nbsp;
vaccinated. If you make between 50 and 100k&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.600
Speaker 2: a year, 77
Speaker 1: percent have been vaccinated. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.749
almost an identical number. Those making over&nbsp;
100k a year, 79 percent have been vaccinated.&nbsp;

00:03:33.749 --> 00:03:37.440
Speaker 2: I mean, essentially no
Speaker 1: impact on vaccination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:43.280
status based on income. So really&nbsp;
interesting numbers and also just&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:49.760
Speaker 2: stunningly low Republican
Speaker 1: vaccination. So at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.200
